# Visual Studio's working files and build output. With the solution and
# the project in one folder, as each demo has them, Visual Studio keeps its
# working files in .vs and in a folder named after the project, and builds
# the program in x64. A pattern that took in every x64 folder would hide
# SDL's own, SDL3\lib\x64, so each demo's folder is named
.vs/
*/x64/
Skeleton/Skeleton/
Plotter/Plotter/
